WEBVTT

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.795
What does it take to turn one part
into a production line?

00:00:07.795 --> 00:00:11.848
Start here, with the raw stock
and the finished Lilt part.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.872
Follow the toolpath through
the first machining operation.

00:00:16.872 --> 00:00:20.208
The next operations are ready to preview.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.019
Inside the cell, follow the part
from one operation to the next.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.074
One finished part reaches
the Lilt pallet.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:39.900
Five work areas. Lilt makes six.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.086
Orange brings in stock.
Red parts move through the cells.

00:00:44.086 --> 00:00:48.693
Blue ships finished product
from an existing work area.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:58.707
In a separate example, review the proposed
handover and the evidence behind it.

00:00:58.707 --> 00:01:02.143
This stays a preview, not a factory release.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.273
Review the draft.

00:01:11.273 --> 00:01:15.534
Select the bore to see its G-code
and machining bill of materials.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.274
Same workload, two forklift layouts.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.925
Modeled travel drops from eleven hundred

00:01:25.925 --> 00:01:29.148
forty-three to four hundred ninety-five
kilometers a year.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.557
The visual check passes.

00:01:34.557 --> 00:01:38.988
The part fails inspection because
its face height is out of tolerance.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:47.514
Raise the planned quantity.
The budget preview now calls for two tools.
